@TUTORIAL: Looking at Output, the Data Set      !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}  The Output Data Set panel shows the output as it would be printed:
}  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------
}  |@SDSF OUTPUT DISPLAY MYJOB    JOB  1240 DSID   102 LINE       1
}  |@COMMAND INPUT ===>                                        SCROLL ===> PAGE
}  |@***************************** TOP OF DATA *****************************
}  | IDCAMS  SYSTEM SERVICES
}  |   LISTCAT LEVEL(HERC01)
}  | NONVSAM ------- HERC01.MYJOB.DATA
}  | IDC0001I FUNCTION COMPLETED, HIGHEST CONDITION CODE WAS 0
}  | IDC0002I IDCAMS PROCESSING COMPLETE. MAXIMUM CONDITION CODE WAS 0
}  |@**************************** BOTTOM OF DATA ***************************
}  +---------------------------------------------------------------------------
}  The title line names the job and the data set at the top (DSID 102);
}  LINE is the line at the top, COLUMNS on the right the columns shown.
{  PF8, PF7    }down and up       {  PF11, PF10  }right and left
{  BOTTOM, TOP }to the end or the start
{  NEXT, PREV  }to the next or the previous data set
}  The End key goes back to the Job Data Set panel.
}
}
}
}  Enter: next   PF10: back   PF7: list of parts   PF3: leave
